    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="Inscr.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ger">Ger</ref> Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Inscr." corresp="#wit-b">[Ger. Inscr.] Be gesceadwisan gerefan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Von einem klugen Amtmann [eines Edelguts].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of a prudent reeve [of a great estate].</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann's text is from B (Cambridge, Corpus Christi College 383, p. 102, after Rect, same hand, c. 1125), the same manuscript as the modern edition; Liebermann treats Gerefa as the continuation of Rect (see Rect 1). There is no Quadripartitus version. The heading is in red. Perhaps the original read ‘Gescadwis’ (Zupitza); B often drops ‘ge-’ (compare 17b).</note>
      </div>
    </body>
